The Windows installer built from this repository (app/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json)
shows LICENSE on its licence page, followed by the terms Microsoft requires
users to accept for the three Visual C++ runtime files in its llama folder
(app/src-tauri/installer-licence.txt), and installs LICENSE, NOTICE,
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the files in licenses/ into a licenses folder
beside the app. Besides this
product's own files it carries the following (licenses/README.md gives the
source and sha256 of each file named):
- llama.cpp (llama-server and its libraries, from llama.cpp's Windows release
  zip; The ggml authors), installed as llama\: MIT
  (licenses/llama.cpp-LICENSE.txt), with the licences of code compiled into
  it: nlohmann/json and cpp-httplib (MIT) and BoringSSL
  (licenses/llama.cpp-*-LICENSE.txt), and of the npm packages in the web page
  llama-server.exe carries (licenses/llama.cpp-webui-npm-packages.txt).
  Beside it: libomp140.x86_64.dll, the LLVM project's OpenMP runtime as
  conda-forge builds it (llvm-openmp 22.1.8), Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions
  (licenses/llvm-openmp-LICENSE.txt); and three files built by Microsoft, the
  Visual C++ runtime, added from Visual Studio 2022 Build Tools, which come
  with no licence text. licenses/msvc-runtime.txt says where they come from
  and quotes what Microsoft says about redistributing them.
- Node.js (Node.js contributors; OpenJS Foundation), installed as node.exe:
  MIT, with the licences of the components it includes
  (licenses/node-LICENSE.txt).
The setup program itself is built from NSIS 3.11 (licenses/NSIS-COPYING.txt)
and Tauri's nsis_tauri_utils.dll (licenses/nsis_tauri_utils-LICENSE_*.txt).
The licence texts of the Rust crates linked into the app, and of the npm
packages its window is bundled from, are in
licenses/rust-crates.txt and licenses/npm-packages.txt.
The app's executable also links Microsoft's WebView2 loader
(WebView2LoaderStatic.lib, through the webview2-com-sys crate):
licenses/Microsoft.Web.WebView2-LICENSE.txt, with the notices file of the package it comes
from, licenses/Microsoft.Web.WebView2-NOTICE.txt.

